{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"extensions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extensions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every built-in extension is available through a separate package entry."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"callouts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callouts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/markdown/extensions/callouts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"calloutsextension","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"calloutsExtension"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function calloutsExtension(): MarkdownExtension","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates the block parser for GitHub-style "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"> [!KIND] Optional title"},{"type":"text","value":" callouts."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parsecalloutblock","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseCalloutBlock"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function parseCalloutBlock(\n  context: BlockParseContext,\n): CalloutNode | undefined","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Low-level parser used by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"calloutsExtension"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"comment-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comment components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/markdown/extensions/comment-components"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"commentcomponentoptions","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CommentComponentOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provides an optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transformComponent(node)"},{"type":"text","value":" callback that receives each parsed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ComponentNode"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"componentcomment","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ComponentComment"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parsed comment data with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"block"},{"type":"text","value":", lowercase "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", and string "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"attributes"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"commentcomponentsextension","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commentComponentsExtension"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function commentComponentsExtension(\n  options?: CommentComponentOptions,\n): MarkdownExtension","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parses single "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<!-- ::name -->"},{"type":"text","value":" comments and paired "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<!-- ::start:name -->"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<!-- ::end:name -->"},{"type":"text","value":" blocks."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parsecommentcomponentblock","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseCommentComponentBlock"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parses a component at the current block context and optionally transforms it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parsecomponentcomment","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseComponentComment"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function parseComponentComment(\n  line: string,\n): ComponentComment | undefined","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parses one component start or single-component comment."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"parseattributes","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseAttributes"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function parseAttributes(value: string): Record<string, string>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parses quoted, unquoted, and boolean-style attributes. A valueless attribute becomes the string "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"true\""},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"docs-preset","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Docs preset"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/markdown/extensions/docs"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"docsmarkdownoptions","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DocsMarkdownOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collectHeadings?: boolean | HeadingCollectionOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"docsmarkdownextensions","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"docsMarkdownExtensions"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function docsMarkdownExtensions(\n  options?: DocsMarkdownOptions,\n): MarkdownExtension[]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns callouts, transformed comment components, and heading collection unless collection is disabled."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"transformdocscomponent","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transformDocsComponent"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Routes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tabs"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"framework"},{"type":"text","value":" component nodes to their built-in transforms and returns other nodes unchanged."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"framework-transform","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Framework transform"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/markdown/extensions/framework"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"transformframeworkcomponent","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transformFrameworkComponent"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function transformFrameworkComponent(\n  node: ComponentNode,\n): ComponentNode","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Splits level-one framework sections into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"md-framework-panel"},{"type":"text","value":" children, records available-framework and code-block metadata, and labels nested headings by framework."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"heading-collection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Heading collection"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/markdown/extensions/headings"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"headingcollectionoptions","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HeadingCollectionOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skipComponentNames?: ReadonlySet<string> | string[]"},{"type":"text","value":". The default skips headings inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tabs"},{"type":"text","value":" components."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"headingcollectionextension","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headingCollectionExtension"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function headingCollectionExtension(\n  options?: HeadingCollectionOptions,\n): MarkdownExtension","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a document transform that writes collected headings to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"document.headings"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"collectmarkdownheadings","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collectMarkdownHeadings"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function collectMarkdownHeadings(\n  document: MarkdownDocument,\n  options?: HeadingCollectionOptions,\n): MarkdownHeading[]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Collects headings recursively through lists, blockquotes, callouts, and components while respecting skipped component names and framework labels."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/markdown/extensions/streaming"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"streamingmarkdownextension","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"streamingMarkdownExtension"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function streamingMarkdownExtension(): MarkdownExtension","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a document transform for accumulated AI responses. The transform removes an empty trailing heading, blockquote, or list item that is likely to be an incomplete block marker. All completed content keeps the core parser's normal output."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tab-transforms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tab transforms"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/markdown/extensions/tabs"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"transformtabscomponent","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transformTabsComponent"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dispatches by the component’s "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"variant"},{"type":"text","value":" attribute. Unknown or missing variants use heading-based tabs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"transformfiletabs","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transformFileTabs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Turns code-block children into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"md-tab-panel"},{"type":"text","value":" elements and records file names, languages, and code in data properties."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"transformpackagemanagertabs","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transformPackageManagerTabs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parses shared "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package..."},{"type":"text","value":" lines and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"framework: package..."},{"type":"text","value":" lines and records package groups plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"install"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dev-install"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"local-install"},{"type":"text","value":" mode. A framework prefix is a name of letters, digits, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-"},{"type":"text","value":" followed by a colon that is not directly followed by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"."},{"type":"text","value":", so URL and path specifiers such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"https://"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file:../"},{"type":"text","value":" stay shared. Each line becomes a separate command group. Unprefixed groups appear under the empty string key in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packagesByFramework"},{"type":"text","value":" and are also included in each named framework's groups, preserving source order."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"transformbundlertabs","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transformBundlerTabs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Selects Vite and Rsbuild heading sections and converts them to panels."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"transformheadingtabs","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transformHeadingTabs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Splits content at the shallowest heading depth, creates stable tab slugs, and emits one panel per section."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The transforms return the original node when their expected input structure is absent."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"extensions","text":"Extensions","level":1},{"id":"callouts","text":"Callouts","level":2},{"id":"calloutsextension","text":"calloutsExtension","level":3},{"id":"parsecalloutblock","text":"parseCalloutBlock","level":3},{"id":"comment-components","text":"Comment components","level":2},{"id":"commentcomponentoptions","text":"CommentComponentOptions","level":3},{"id":"componentcomment","text":"ComponentComment","level":3},{"id":"commentcomponentsextension","text":"commentComponentsExtension","level":3},{"id":"parsecommentcomponentblock","text":"parseCommentComponentBlock","level":3},{"id":"parsecomponentcomment","text":"parseComponentComment","level":3},{"id":"parseattributes","text":"parseAttributes","level":3},{"id":"docs-preset","text":"Docs preset","level":2},{"id":"docsmarkdownoptions","text":"DocsMarkdownOptions","level":3},{"id":"docsmarkdownextensions","text":"docsMarkdownExtensions","level":3},{"id":"transformdocscomponent","text":"transformDocsComponent","level":3},{"id":"framework-transform","text":"Framework transform","level":2},{"id":"transformframeworkcomponent","text":"transformFrameworkComponent","level":3},{"id":"heading-collection","text":"Heading collection","level":2},{"id":"headingcollectionoptions","text":"HeadingCollectionOptions","level":3},{"id":"headingcollectionextension","text":"headingCollectionExtension","level":3},{"id":"collectmarkdownheadings","text":"collectMarkdownHeadings","level":3},{"id":"streaming","text":"Streaming","level":2},{"id":"streamingmarkdownextension","text":"streamingMarkdownExtension","level":3},{"id":"tab-transforms","text":"Tab transforms","level":2},{"id":"transformtabscomponent","text":"transformTabsComponent","level":3},{"id":"transformfiletabs","text":"transformFileTabs","level":3},{"id":"transformpackagemanagertabs","text":"transformPackageManagerTabs","level":3},{"id":"transformbundlertabs","text":"transformBundlerTabs","level":3},{"id":"transformheadingtabs","text":"transformHeadingTabs","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Extensions\n\nEvery built-in extension is available through a separate package entry.\n\n## Callouts\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/callouts`.\n\n### `calloutsExtension`\n\n```ts\nfunction calloutsExtension(): MarkdownExtension\n```\n\nCreates the block parser for GitHub-style `> [!KIND] Optional title` callouts.\n\n### `parseCalloutBlock`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseCalloutBlock(\n  context: BlockParseContext,\n): CalloutNode | undefined\n```\n\nLow-level parser used by `calloutsExtension`.\n\n## Comment components\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/comment-components`.\n\n### `CommentComponentOptions`\n\nProvides an optional `transformComponent(node)` callback that receives each parsed `ComponentNode`.\n\n### `ComponentComment`\n\nParsed comment data with `block`, lowercase `name`, and string `attributes`.\n\n### `commentComponentsExtension`\n\n```ts\nfunction commentComponentsExtension(\n  options?: CommentComponentOptions,\n): MarkdownExtension\n```\n\nParses single `<!-- ::name -->` comments and paired `<!-- ::start:name -->` / `<!-- ::end:name -->` blocks.\n\n### `parseCommentComponentBlock`\n\nParses a component at the current block context and optionally transforms it.\n\n### `parseComponentComment`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseComponentComment(\n  line: string,\n): ComponentComment | undefined\n```\n\nParses one component start or single-component comment.\n\n### `parseAttributes`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseAttributes(value: string): Record<string, string>\n```\n\nParses quoted, unquoted, and boolean-style attributes. A valueless attribute becomes the string `\"true\"`.\n\n## Docs preset\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/docs`.\n\n### `DocsMarkdownOptions`\n\nContains `collectHeadings?: boolean | HeadingCollectionOptions`.\n\n### `docsMarkdownExtensions`\n\n```ts\nfunction docsMarkdownExtensions(\n  options?: DocsMarkdownOptions,\n): MarkdownExtension[]\n```\n\nReturns callouts, transformed comment components, and heading collection unless collection is disabled.\n\n### `transformDocsComponent`\n\nRoutes `tabs` and `framework` component nodes to their built-in transforms and returns other nodes unchanged.\n\n## Framework transform\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/framework`.\n\n### `transformFrameworkComponent`\n\n```ts\nfunction transformFrameworkComponent(\n  node: ComponentNode,\n): ComponentNode\n```\n\nSplits level-one framework sections into `md-framework-panel` children, records available-framework and code-block metadata, and labels nested headings by framework.\n\n## Heading collection\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/headings`.\n\n### `HeadingCollectionOptions`\n\nContains `skipComponentNames?: ReadonlySet<string> | string[]`. The default skips headings inside `tabs` components.\n\n### `headingCollectionExtension`\n\n```ts\nfunction headingCollectionExtension(\n  options?: HeadingCollectionOptions,\n): MarkdownExtension\n```\n\nCreates a document transform that writes collected headings to `document.headings`.\n\n### `collectMarkdownHeadings`\n\n```ts\nfunction collectMarkdownHeadings(\n  document: MarkdownDocument,\n  options?: HeadingCollectionOptions,\n): MarkdownHeading[]\n```\n\nCollects headings recursively through lists, blockquotes, callouts, and components while respecting skipped component names and framework labels.\n\n## Streaming\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/streaming`.\n\n### `streamingMarkdownExtension`\n\n```ts\nfunction streamingMarkdownExtension(): MarkdownExtension\n```\n\nCreates a document transform for accumulated AI responses. The transform removes an empty trailing heading, blockquote, or list item that is likely to be an incomplete block marker. All completed content keeps the core parser's normal output.\n\n## Tab transforms\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/tabs`.\n\n### `transformTabsComponent`\n\nDispatches by the component’s `variant` attribute. Unknown or missing variants use heading-based tabs.\n\n### `transformFileTabs`\n\nTurns code-block children into `md-tab-panel` elements and records file names, languages, and code in data properties.\n\n### `transformPackageManagerTabs`\n\nParses shared `package...` lines and `framework: package...` lines and records package groups plus `install`, `dev-install`, or `local-install` mode. A framework prefix is a name of letters, digits, `_`, or `-` followed by a colon that is not directly followed by `/` or `.`, so URL and path specifiers such as `https://` and `file:../` stay shared. Each line becomes a separate command group. Unprefixed groups appear under the empty string key in `packagesByFramework` and are also included in each named framework's groups, preserving source order.\n\n### `transformBundlerTabs`\n\nSelects Vite and Rsbuild heading sections and converts them to panels.\n\n### `transformHeadingTabs`\n\nSplits content at the shallowest heading depth, creates stable tab slugs, and emits one panel per section.\n\nThe transforms return the original node when their expected input structure is absent.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Extensions\n---\n\n# Extensions\n\nEvery built-in extension is available through a separate package entry.\n\n## Callouts\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/callouts`.\n\n### `calloutsExtension`\n\n```ts\nfunction calloutsExtension(): MarkdownExtension\n```\n\nCreates the block parser for GitHub-style `> [!KIND] Optional title` callouts.\n\n### `parseCalloutBlock`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseCalloutBlock(\n  context: BlockParseContext,\n): CalloutNode | undefined\n```\n\nLow-level parser used by `calloutsExtension`.\n\n## Comment components\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/comment-components`.\n\n### `CommentComponentOptions`\n\nProvides an optional `transformComponent(node)` callback that receives each parsed `ComponentNode`.\n\n### `ComponentComment`\n\nParsed comment data with `block`, lowercase `name`, and string `attributes`.\n\n### `commentComponentsExtension`\n\n```ts\nfunction commentComponentsExtension(\n  options?: CommentComponentOptions,\n): MarkdownExtension\n```\n\nParses single `<!-- ::name -->` comments and paired `<!-- ::start:name -->` / `<!-- ::end:name -->` blocks.\n\n### `parseCommentComponentBlock`\n\nParses a component at the current block context and optionally transforms it.\n\n### `parseComponentComment`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseComponentComment(\n  line: string,\n): ComponentComment | undefined\n```\n\nParses one component start or single-component comment.\n\n### `parseAttributes`\n\n```ts\nfunction parseAttributes(value: string): Record<string, string>\n```\n\nParses quoted, unquoted, and boolean-style attributes. A valueless attribute becomes the string `\"true\"`.\n\n## Docs preset\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/docs`.\n\n### `DocsMarkdownOptions`\n\nContains `collectHeadings?: boolean | HeadingCollectionOptions`.\n\n### `docsMarkdownExtensions`\n\n```ts\nfunction docsMarkdownExtensions(\n  options?: DocsMarkdownOptions,\n): MarkdownExtension[]\n```\n\nReturns callouts, transformed comment components, and heading collection unless collection is disabled.\n\n### `transformDocsComponent`\n\nRoutes `tabs` and `framework` component nodes to their built-in transforms and returns other nodes unchanged.\n\n## Framework transform\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/framework`.\n\n### `transformFrameworkComponent`\n\n```ts\nfunction transformFrameworkComponent(\n  node: ComponentNode,\n): ComponentNode\n```\n\nSplits level-one framework sections into `md-framework-panel` children, records available-framework and code-block metadata, and labels nested headings by framework.\n\n## Heading collection\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/headings`.\n\n### `HeadingCollectionOptions`\n\nContains `skipComponentNames?: ReadonlySet<string> | string[]`. The default skips headings inside `tabs` components.\n\n### `headingCollectionExtension`\n\n```ts\nfunction headingCollectionExtension(\n  options?: HeadingCollectionOptions,\n): MarkdownExtension\n```\n\nCreates a document transform that writes collected headings to `document.headings`.\n\n### `collectMarkdownHeadings`\n\n```ts\nfunction collectMarkdownHeadings(\n  document: MarkdownDocument,\n  options?: HeadingCollectionOptions,\n): MarkdownHeading[]\n```\n\nCollects headings recursively through lists, blockquotes, callouts, and components while respecting skipped component names and framework labels.\n\n## Streaming\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/streaming`.\n\n### `streamingMarkdownExtension`\n\n```ts\nfunction streamingMarkdownExtension(): MarkdownExtension\n```\n\nCreates a document transform for accumulated AI responses. The transform removes an empty trailing heading, blockquote, or list item that is likely to be an incomplete block marker. All completed content keeps the core parser's normal output.\n\n## Tab transforms\n\nImport from `@tanstack/markdown/extensions/tabs`.\n\n### `transformTabsComponent`\n\nDispatches by the component’s `variant` attribute. Unknown or missing variants use heading-based tabs.\n\n### `transformFileTabs`\n\nTurns code-block children into `md-tab-panel` elements and records file names, languages, and code in data properties.\n\n### `transformPackageManagerTabs`\n\nParses shared `package...` lines and `framework: package...` lines and records package groups plus `install`, `dev-install`, or `local-install` mode. A framework prefix is a name of letters, digits, `_`, or `-` followed by a colon that is not directly followed by `/` or `.`, so URL and path specifiers such as `https://` and `file:../` stay shared. Each line becomes a separate command group. Unprefixed groups appear under the empty string key in `packagesByFramework` and are also included in each named framework's groups, preserving source order.\n\n### `transformBundlerTabs`\n\nSelects Vite and Rsbuild heading sections and converts them to panels.\n\n### `transformHeadingTabs`\n\nSplits content at the shallowest heading depth, creates stable tab slugs, and emits one panel per section.\n\nThe transforms return the original node when their expected input structure is absent.\n"}
